    description: "Follow-up to WI-fozoh (split from its Plan A / Plan B comparison; Plan A\nshipped in PR #3355). Plan A canonicalised the synthesis side: every\nboundary Symbol now carries `stable_id`/`canonical_name`, and `kind=\"file\"`\npseudo-IDs collapse per language. Plan A is sufficient for WI-fozoh's\nstated symptom but does not address the **structural cause** of the file-id\nexternals — which this item exists to fix.\n\n## Symptom (residual)\n\nThe 732 file-named boundary nodes on hypergumbo self-analysis collapse\nto 1 under Plan A, but they're synthesized in the first place because\nanalyzers emit import edges with `src=make_file_id(path)` while the\nmatching module Symbol uses a different id format (`{lang}:{path}:1-{end}:<module:{name}>:module`).\nEvery Python file's import-edge `src` is therefore dangling at synthesis\ntime — Plan A canonicalises the dangling, but the edges still go through\n`create_boundary_nodes` rather than landing on a real producer-side\nSymbol.\n\nPlan B's Phase 1 audit identified ~20 affected analyzers across\n`lang-mainstream`, `lang-common`, and `lang-extended1`: Python, C, C++,\nPerl, Bash, Proto, Thrift, plus ~13 in lang-common / lang-extended1.\nSome analyzers (Go, Java, Rust, Lua, HTML, JS/TS) already emit a matching\nfile pseudo-symbol and are unaffected.\n\n## Recommended approach: centralized post-process\n\nThe original Plan B proposal was per-analyzer fixes — emit a real file\nSymbol in each affected analyzer's pass. Two cheaper alternatives:\n\n1. **Centralized post-process at result-collection time.** The\n   orchestrator already iterates analyzer results in\n   `run_all_analyzers`. A single post-processing pass there can scan\n   each `AnalysisResult` for edges whose `src`/`dst` match\n   `make_file_id(path)` shape and auto-synthesize a real file Symbol\n   with that id, before the result enters the global graph. **One\n   place to fix; all affected analyzers benefit; no per-analyzer\n   ceremony.** This is essentially \"Plan B at the chokepoint\" — same\n   structural restoration of \"every edge endpoint resolves to a real\n   Symbol,\" without per-analyzer churn.\n\n2. **Parameterized invariant test as guard.** Iterate\n   `_registry_get_all()`, run each analyzer on a minimal synthetic\n   input, assert no `edge.src`/`edge.dst` is dangling within the\n   analyzer's own results. Auto-discovers the failing set without\n   grepping the 90+ analyzer source files. The empirical count may\n   be smaller than the audit's 20+; whatever it is, that's the\n   actual work surface.\n\nRecommendation: implement #1 (centralized post-process) and add #2 as\na regression guard.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nAfter this lands:\n\n- The canonical `python:<external>:0-0:file:file` boundary Symbol is no\n  longer synthesized on hypergumbo self-analysis (drops from 1 to 0\n  under Plan A's count).\n- Every `make_file_id`-style edge endpoint resolves to a real file\n  Symbol emitted by the orchestrator's post-process step (or, when the\n  analyzer already emits one, that one).\n- The new invariant test `test_no_dangling_make_file_id_endpoints`\n  passes for every registered analyzer.\n- An invariant tracker item `INV-make-file-id-emits-symbol` is filed\n  alongside this WI to keep future analyzers compliant.\n\n## Schema impact\n\nAdding `kind=\"file\"` to the `Symbol.kind` enum in `docs/schema.json` is\nlikely needed (additive, patch-bump per ADR-0014). Confirm before\nimplementing — the centralized synthesis can use whatever kind the\nexisting analyzers' file Symbols use, which may already be in the enum.\n\n## Validation\n\n1. `pytest` — green, 100% coverage on changed files.\n2. **Self-analysis dogfood**: `hypergumbo run . --out /tmp/hg.json`\n   then assert the JSON has no `external_symbol` node named `\"file\"`.\n3. **Cross-language check** on a polyglot repo with at least one\n   affected language (C, Perl, Bash) confirming the same.\n4. **Bakeoff-deep cycle** to confirm no centrality regression — file\n   Symbols become real nodes with non-trivial in-degree from import\n   edges, which could perturb sketch ranking.\n\nTag `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge time; claim is \"the\ncanonical-file boundary Symbol is no longer synthesized on hypergumbo\nor any tested polyglot repo.\"\n\n## Risks and mitigations\n\n- **High in-degree on file Symbols** could distort centrality. Plan\n  A's `variable`-kind language-conditional noise filter (WI-gafog) is\n  the precedent for fixing this if needed: gate file pseudo-symbols\n  out of ranking when they're zero-information, keep them in for\n  containment / file-level metrics.\n- **Schema bump**: additive only, but governance-touching. Verify the\n  `Symbol.kind` enum already accommodates `\"file\"` (it may not, per\n  the current schema dump).\n\n## Relationship to Plan A (PR #3355)\n\nPlan A canonicalises and dedupes; Plan B (this item) fixes the\nproducer side so canonicalisation isn't needed for file-id externals\nin the first place. Once both land, the boundary-synthesis layer is\nboth *narrow* (only genuine externals) and *identity-bearing* (every\nboundary node has stable_id/canonical_name from Plan A).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Per-analyzer audits to find other dangling-id classes beyond\n  `make_file_id`. The invariant test in #2 will catch these\n  empirically; address each as a follow-up if it surfaces.\n- `module` pseudo-symbols (203 on hypergumbo self-analysis) are\n  semantically meaningful — each represents a distinct imported\n  module — and intentionally NOT collapsed by Plan A. They don't\n  participate in this work item."  # 837b
    fields: {}  # 837b
- op: update  # 4d5c
  at: '2026-04-25T08:43:24Z'  # 4d5c
  by: agent  # 4d5c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4d5c
  clock: 2  # 4d5c
  nonce: 4d5c  # 4d5c
  set:  # 4d5c
    description: "Follow-up to WI-fozoh (split from its Plan A / Plan B comparison; Plan A\nshipped in PR #3355). Plan A canonicalised the synthesis side: every\nboundary Symbol now carries `stable_id`/`canonical_name`, and `kind=\"file\"`\npseudo-IDs collapse per language. Plan A is sufficient for WI-fozoh's\nstated symptom but does not address the **structural cause** of the file-id\nexternals — which this item exists to fix.\n\n## Symptom (residual)\n\nThe 732 file-named boundary nodes on hypergumbo self-analysis collapse\nto 1 under Plan A, but they're synthesized in the first place because\nanalyzers emit import edges with `src=make_file_id(path)` while the\nmatching module Symbol uses a different id format (`{lang}:{path}:1-{end}:<module:{name}>:module`).\nEvery Python file's import-edge `src` is therefore dangling at synthesis\ntime — Plan A canonicalises the dangling, but the edges still go through\n`create_boundary_nodes` rather than landing on a real producer-side\nSymbol.\n\nPlan B's Phase 1 audit identified ~20 affected analyzers across\n`lang-mainstream`, `lang-common`, and `lang-extended1`: Python, C, C++,\nPerl, Bash, Proto, Thrift, plus ~13 in lang-common / lang-extended1.\nSome analyzers (Go, Java, Rust, Lua, HTML, JS/TS) already emit a matching\nfile pseudo-symbol and are unaffected.\n\n## Empirically-confirmed scope (2026-04-25 self-analysis dogfood)\n\nInstrumented `_parse_dangling_id` and ran the full pipeline on\nhypergumbo itself. Findings:\n\n- **2,152 import / imports_module / depends_on_manifest edges** are\n  sourced from file-named external boundaries today (1 python +\n  5 typescript file externals). That's effectively **100 % of the\n  imports edge population in the JSON output** (2,132 imports / 2,132\n  total).\n- After Plan A's `apply_external_id_remap` rewrites + tuple-dedup,\n  the imports edge count drops 14,149 → 2,136 — a **6.6× collapse**\n  in apparent import volume. Per-file attribution survives only via\n  `meta.referring_paths` (capped at 50), so widely-imported modules\n  silently lose attribution beyond the first 50 importers.\n- WI-ramuv would **reverse this drop** — the ~12,000 collapsed edges\n  reappear as distinct (file_X → module_Y) edges with native per-file\n  src, and the 50-cap loss disappears.\n\nThis is the upside, but it's also the centrality risk the noise-filter\ndeliverable below addresses.\n\n## Recommended approach: centralized post-process + noise-filter (co-required)\n\nThe original Plan B proposal was per-analyzer fixes — emit a real file\nSymbol in each affected analyzer's pass. Two cheaper alternatives:\n\n1. **Centralized post-process at result-collection time.** The\n   orchestrator already iterates analyzer results in\n   `run_all_analyzers`. A single post-processing pass there can scan\n   each `AnalysisResult` for edges whose `src`/`dst` match\n   `make_file_id(path)` shape and auto-synthesize a real file Symbol\n   with that id, before the result enters the global graph. **One\n   place to fix; all affected analyzers benefit; no per-analyzer\n   ceremony.** This is essentially \"Plan B at the chokepoint\" — same\n   structural restoration of \"every edge endpoint resolves to a real\n   Symbol,\" without per-analyzer churn.\n\n2. **Parameterized invariant test as guard.** Iterate\n   `_registry_get_all()`, run each analyzer on a minimal synthetic\n   input, assert no `edge.src`/`edge.dst` is dangling within the\n   analyzer's own results. Auto-discovers the failing set without\n   grepping the 90+ analyzer source files. The empirical count may\n   be smaller than the audit's 20+; whatever it is, that's the\n   actual work surface.\n\n3. **Centrality noise-filter (CO-REQUIRED, not optional).** Once\n   ~700–2,000 file Symbols enter the graph (one per analyzed source\n   file across the affected languages), each will have an in-degree\n   equal to the number of imports inside that file (typically 5–50\n   for Python). That displaces today's top-ranked symbols (`Symbol`\n   class with degree 389, `find_files` with 281, `TreeSitterAnalyzer`\n   with 231) in centrality-ranked output. The fix is a\n   language-conditional noise filter for `kind=\"file\"` mirroring\n   WI-gafog's `kind=\"variable\"` exclusion — gate file Symbols out of\n   ranking while keeping them in for containment, slice traversal,\n   and per-file metrics. **Must ship in the same PR as the\n   post-process** — landing #1 without #3 introduces a deterministic\n   sketch-ranking regression on day one.\n\nRecommendation: implement #1 (centralized post-process) AND #3\n(noise-filter) together, with #2 as the regression guard.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\nAfter this lands (all four required, in one PR):\n\n- [#1] The canonical `python:<external>:0-0:file:file` boundary Symbol\n  is no longer synthesized on hypergumbo self-analysis (drops from 1\n  to 0 under Plan A's count).\n- [#1] Every `make_file_id`-style edge endpoint resolves to a real\n  file Symbol emitted by the orchestrator's post-process step (or,\n  when the analyzer already emits one, that one).\n- [#2] The new invariant test `test_no_dangling_make_file_id_endpoints`\n  passes for every registered analyzer.\n- [#2] An invariant tracker item `INV-make-file-id-emits-symbol` is\n  filed alongside this WI to keep future analyzers compliant.\n- [#3] Sketch ranking on hypergumbo self-analysis: top-30 contains\n  zero `kind=\"file\"` Symbols (with the noise-filter active). The\n  current top-30 (Symbol, find_files, Span, iter_tree,\n  TreeSitterAnalyzer, register_analyzer, …) is preserved within ±3\n  positions.\n- [#3] The noise filter is language-conditional (mirrors WI-gafog's\n  `{css, scss, sass, less}` precedent) so any future language whose\n  file Symbols ARE semantically meaningful as ranking entries can opt\n  back in via the same allow-list mechanism.\n\n## Schema impact\n\nAdding `kind=\"file\"` to the `Symbol.kind` enum in `docs/schema.json` is\nlikely needed (additive, patch-bump per ADR-0014). Confirm before\nimplementing — the centralized synthesis can use whatever kind the\nexisting analyzers' file Symbols use, which may already be in the enum.\n\n## Validation\n\n1. `pytest` — green, 100% coverage on changed files (covers #1, #2, #3).\n2. **Self-analysis dogfood**: `hypergumbo run . --out /tmp/hg.json`\n   then assert:\n   - JSON has no `external_symbol` node named `\"file\"` (#1).\n   - Imports edge count rises from current 2,136 toward ~14,149 with\n     full per-file src attribution (#1 side-effect, see \"Empirically-\n     confirmed scope\" above).\n   - Sketch top-30 contains zero `kind=\"file\"` Symbols (#3).\n3. **Cross-language check** on a polyglot repo with at least one\n   affected language (C, Perl, Bash) confirming the same.\n4. **Bakeoff-deep cycle** to confirm no centrality regression on the\n   diverse-repo corpus and to revalidate WI-fozoh's \"37% drop in\n   external-symbol count\" claim under the new regime (the denominator\n   changes when ~700+ file Symbols enter the corpus).\n\nTag `awaits_bakeoff_validation` at merge time; claim is \"the\ncanonical-file boundary Symbol is no longer synthesized on hypergumbo\nor any tested polyglot repo, AND sketch ranking is structurally\nunchanged on the bakeoff corpus.\"\n\n## Risks and mitigations\n\n- **High in-degree on file Symbols** would deterministically distort\n  centrality if shipped without the noise-filter. **Mitigated by the\n  co-required deliverable #3 above** — not optional. WI-gafog's\n  `kind=\"variable\"` language-conditional exclusion is the working\n  precedent.\n- **Schema bump**: additive only, but governance-touching. Verify the\n  `Symbol.kind` enum already accommodates `\"file\"` (it may not, per\n  the current schema dump).\n- **Bakeoff revalidation of WI-fozoh's count claim** — the\n  external_symbol denominator changes; need to revisit that\n  `awaits_bakeoff_validation` tag at the same cycle.\n\n## Relationship to Plan A (PR #3355)\n\nPlan A canonicalises and dedupes; Plan B (this item) fixes the\nproducer side so canonicalisation isn't needed for file-id externals\nin the first place. Once both land, the boundary-synthesis layer is\nboth *narrow* (only genuine externals) and *identity-bearing* (every\nboundary node has stable_id/canonical_name from Plan A).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Per-analyzer audits to find other dangling-id classes beyond\n  `make_file_id`. The invariant test in #2 will catch these\n  empirically; address each as a follow-up if it surfaces.\n- `module` pseudo-symbols (203 on hypergumbo self-analysis) are\n  semantically meaningful — each represents a distinct imported\n  module — and intentionally NOT collapsed by Plan A. They don't\n  participate in this work item.\n- Promoting \"imports-out-degree\" to a first-class ranking signal —\n  separate item if/when the use case surfaces."  # 4d5c
